MVNO Graduation Demo — Audit & Real-Flow Hardening Run (2026-08-08)
===================================================================
Session: DeepSeek live-agent audit of "remove simulations -> real interactive flows".

The audit proposed removing product-logic simulations used as evidence. Investigation
empirically reframed the top blocker and hardened every flagged evidence step to REAL
behavior. All gates re-verified live.

----------------------------------------------------------------------
1. RTP BLOCKER RESOLVED (was a decode-artifact false alarm)
----------------------------------------------------------------------
Handoff claimed the containerized baresip call produced "no RTP packets"
(`tshark -r <pcap> -Y rtp` = 0). Root cause: RTPEngine (drachtio mr9.4.0.0)
records pcap in `eth` format on ephemeral relay ports (e.g. UDP 30010-30050);
Wireshark's UDP->RTP heuristic does NOT auto-decode those ports, so -Y rtp reports
0 while the frames are 172-byte G.711 PCMU.

Forcing decode reveals media IS pinned through RTPEngine:
  - pcap 5aa83f5f… (early run): 703 RTP (caller->RTPEngine:30000) + 117 RTP (callee->30094)
  - pcap e4829224… (fresh run):  692 (caller->30050) + 195 (callee->30032)
  - tshark -d udp.port==30000,rtp yields RTP PT=ITU-T G.711 PCMU, so on
  - live_tap.sh --once uses data.data (not -Y rtp) and extracts per-leg WAVs fine.

Conclusion: media never stopped traversing RTPEngine; the demo now documents
that `-Y rtp` needs the decode directive and that live_tap is the extraction path.

----------------------------------------------------------------------
2. [5c] REAL CALL RECORDING -> WAV -> Vosk TRANSCRIPT (verified fresh)
----------------------------------------------------------------------
demo_call.sh setup+dial -> full baresip lifecycle through Kamailio:
  CALL_OUTGOING -> CALL_RINGING -> CALL_ANSWERED -> CALL_ESTABLISHED
  -> CALL_RTPESTAB(sendrecv) -> CALL_CLOSED ; rx answers = 1
Fresh pcap e4829224…: 192512 bytes. live_tap.sh --once -> callee leg 3.9s WAV,
caller leg 14.1s WAV. Vosk transcribed the callee leg of the LIVE call:
  { "text" : "you have won a prime target how are your account will be close" }

Hardening: demo_call.sh now renders the canned callee phrase longer
("You have won a prize, call us now or your account will be closed", 3.89 s)
so the [5c] WAV-duration >=3s floor holds on the speech-bearing callee leg;
the runbook [5c] now picks the NON-EMPTY leg (never the silent caller leg).

----------------------------------------------------------------------
3. [8] USER SMS -> REAL SMPP MO (OsmoSMSC) -> REST INTERCEPT (new)
----------------------------------------------------------------------
Replaced the pure-REST curl bypass with the real mobile-originated SMPP path:
  send_smpp_sms.py SUBMIT_SM -> OsmoSMSC (2775) -> smsc.db
  BIND_TRANSCEIVER ESME_ROK; SUBMIT_SM ESME_ROK; row lands in smsc.db (GSM-7
  packed user_data, empty text column). The user-supplied nonce is recovered
  from smsc.db via ip_sm_gw.gsm7_decode — proving the user's exact SMS traversed
  the SMSC for real, then the REST intercept classifies it Clean.
SMS text: env $SMS_TEXT > interactive TTY prompt > default. Screenshot of the
run: nonce MVNO5G-1786139807 confirmed in smsc.db via GSM-7 decode; REST
allow=true, reason=Clean content.

----------------------------------------------------------------------
4. [9] Vosk ASR ON THE REAL RECORDED CALL (was a synthetic 350Hz sine wave)
----------------------------------------------------------------------
Removed the Python-generated 350Hz beep. [9] now re-arches the real recorded
[5c] callee WAV into the spool; NativeVoskService decodes and archives it.
Verified: seeded WAV -> archived transcript "you have won a prime target how are
your account will be close" (non-empty) within the poll window.

----------------------------------------------------------------------
5. [9b] REAL SCAM VERDICT (was espeak-ng TTS + hardcoded fixture replay)
----------------------------------------------------------------------
Removed espeak-ng TTS synthesis and the hardcoded live-385288… fixture replay.
[9b] now re-arches THIS run's real recorded scam WAV, echoes the real Vosk
transcript, asserts a scam keyword is present, and waits for
mvno_vosk_blocked_total to increment. Verified live:
  transcript: "you have won a prime target how are your account will be close"
  scam keyword 'won' present; mvno_vosk_blocked_total 6 -> 7  (genuine phishing verdict)

