6. demo_call.sh live-mic prompt
----------------------------------------------------------------------
`dial` now, when the host Pulse socket is present AND stdin is a TTY, prompts the
operator to SPEAK the scam phrase into the live microphone during a 12s countdown
(the caller leg already uses pulse), so the caller leg captures YOUR real voice.
Non-TTY / no-mic falls back to the canned callee phrase (deterministic guard).

